From f2f58e5a580b9ba49de7563b6e32d4206381b270 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:33:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phase3-audit: fire-pass simplifications + named mechanism
 margins (C-tier)

RangedFireProcessor.cpp:
- The A14 GAS mirror (interim writer, UnitSync owns it Phase 4+) now does
  ONE TActorIterator sweep per pass into a cached unit->actor map -- was a
  per-unit scan, O(units x actors) per tick on the game thread.
- The blocker-query radius reads the seam's ONE impact-zone formula
  (ImpactZoneRadiusForDist, new in BattleRanged) plus a named pad -- was a
  re-typed derivation of the same cone math.
- The overlay bar + mirror fractions read the seam's ComputeAmmoFraction --
  was two hand-rolled divisions with their own Max(1,...) guards.
- The skirmish facing fetch reads State->Roster (already in hand) instead
  of a redundant registry FindRoster.
- The pool TTL write reads FRangedConstants::TtlSafetyMarginS (was 2.f).

BattleRanged.h/.cpp: FRangedConstants::TtlSafetyMarginS + the
ImpactZoneRadiusForDist helper (ONE formula for the seam's zone count and
the fire pass's query); the two 0.3f LOS-clearance sites read
FBallisticsConstants::LosClearanceM (BattleBallistics.h). The pool
reserve floor is named (BattleProjectileSubsystem.cpp, was Max(16, ...)).

Values identical at every site; the mirror's per-pass cost is the only
behavior-adjacent change (same writes, fewer scans).

MUST re-run on the UE machine: full unit + func tier (the fire pass feeds
S6/Skirmish/PerfStress; expected green, same EXEC_RESULT lines).
